      ":question/problem": "Given the set of functions ${x,\\,{e}^{x},\\,2x}$ defined on $x\\in R,$ select the correct options in the following reasoning.For all $x\\in R,$  we have that\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}\\cdot x+{{field-2}}\\cdot {e}^{x}+{{field-3}}\\cdot 2x=0.\n$$\n\nSince \n{{field-4}} \nthe scalar coefficients in the linear combination are zero, the given set of functions is linearly \n{{field-5}}."
