      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-334026",
      ":question/problem": "Given the set of functions ${{e}^{x},\\,x}$ defined on $x\\in R,$ select the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\nSuppose for all $x\\in R,$ we have that \n\n$$\n{k}_{1}\\cdot {e}^{x}+{k}_{2}\\cdot x=0,\n$$\n\nwhere ${k}_{1}$ and ${k}_{2}$ are constants.\n\nFor example:\n\n$\\,$\nIf $x=0,$ we get  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$\nIf $x=\\operatorname{ln}\u20612,$ we get  \n{{field-2}}.\n\nThus, we obtain the following system of linear equations:  \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{k}_{1}=0 \\\\ 2{k}_{1}+(\\operatorname{ln}\u20612){k}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe only solution for this system is {{field-3}}.\n\nSince \n{{field-4}} \nthe scalar coefficients in the linear combination are zero, the given set of functions is linearly \n{{field-5}}."
